From 2dcee4b6d796cfef00bd18f10b78fe7bc8061a6e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Book Buddy Handoff <handoff@bookbuddy.local>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 01:32:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] feat(marketplace): shared UI components (browse, sell,
 express interest)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Client components under components/marketplace/, each doing its own
RLS-scoped data fetching via lib/supabase/client — same pattern as
MessagesInbox:

- BrowseListings / ListingCard / CategoryBadge / RecommendedListings
- ListingForm (create + edit, uploads photos to the
  marketplace-listing-photos Storage bucket) / MyListingsPanel
- ListingDetail — the key change from the earlier design: instead of a
  buy/checkout flow, a non-owner sees an 'Express interest' box that
  calls the existing create_conversation() RPC and posts an opening
  message, then points them at the normal Messages inbox to work out
  payment and delivery themselves.
- MarketplaceSubNav — now just Browse / Sell (no Orders tab, no
  seller-action badge — there's nothing for a seller to 'act on' until
  payments exist).
